  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "FedoraObjectResource around line 264:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If the ingested file is AtomZip, there's a check that the MIMEType is XML-compatible - this won't usually be the case for AtomZip.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If the test fails, the stream is left as null, and a new blank object is created.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The logic should be changed so that if a binary ingest format has been specified, this check for XML mime type is skipped.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Work-around is to specifty the parameter ignoreMime=true",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Can be tested using the web admin client - export an object in AtomZIP format, then try ingesting it; you'll get an NPE (as the ZIP file being read at this point isn't a zip file, it's the template FOXML file created due to the MIME check above resulting in a null inputstream and therefore a template FOXML file being created).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
